infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Continuous vs triggered fitness functions
  desc Match each check's cost to its frequency: cheap structural checks gate every commit, expensive emergent checks run on a schedule
  compares
    - label Continuous
      children
        - label Runs on every commit
          desc In the development loop, as fast as possible
        - label Cost: ~2 seconds
          desc ArchUnit cyclic-dependency check in the unit suite
        - label Source-only, no build
          desc Evaluated against source code — no deploy needed
        - label Structural properties
          desc Dependency rules, cycles, import restrictions
        - label Zero detection lag
          desc Fails the moment the boundary is crossed
    - label Triggered
      children
        - label Runs on schedule or event
          desc On demand — in CI, on merge, nightly, pre-release
        - label Cost: minutes (8-min load test)
          desc Too slow to gate every commit without killing velocity
        - label Needs a built artifact
          desc Requires a running or staging environment
        - label Emergent properties
          desc Load tests, full security scans, integration tests
        - label Tolerates a feedback lag
          desc p99 < 200ms at 10,000 RPM, checked nightly
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f59e0b
